1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,900
A bid is a promise.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,500
Most bids cost nothing. A film by Harsh Bhanushali and Dhairya Patel.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:12,000
GAVEL. Every bid is a hold. The hammer is the payment.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,800
Charge first, bidders hold back.

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,100
No hold, winners walk away.

6
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,500
Paper sheets, no proof.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,200
A ceiling.

8
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,200
Bids under it.

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,800
Capture the winner.

10
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:30,000
Release the rest. Orders v2 intent AUTHORIZE; Payments v2 capture with final_capture, void.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,300
Open /try. One tap. One sandbox room.

12
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,700
A code. A QR.

13
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:46,200
Type the code. Or scan the QR.

14
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:52,682
Pick a ceiling.

15
00:00:52,882 --> 00:00:56,981
Hold 3 seconds.

16
00:00:57,081 --> 00:00:59,700
Held, not charged.

17
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,800
Open the lot.

18
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,757
Bids arrive.

19
00:01:06,857 --> 00:01:10,495
Only up.

20
00:01:10,595 --> 00:01:14,700
Every screen agrees.

21
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,600
Or say it.

22
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,800
"three fifty for paddle twelve"

23
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,000
amount 350.00, paddle 12

24
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,500
Did you mean $350 for paddle 12? Confirm. Illustration: speech is measured on 24 synthetic clips only (G5 partial).

25
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:28,392
Hold the hammer. 3 seconds. No accidents.

26
00:01:28,492 --> 00:01:30,800
Sold.

27
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,200
The screen names the winner.

28
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,900
Capture only the winning price.

29
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:43,500
Release every other hold. Drawn, not recorded: real sandbox capture and void are proven in G1 and G4.

30
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:47,100
A receipt for everyone.

31
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,700
Share link. QR.

32
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:55,159
Paste the export.

33
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:59,527
Chain verified. Then one entry is edited.

34
00:01:59,627 --> 00:02:01,200
Chain broken.

35
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,300
Kill survived. A real server kill during settlement on the PayPal sandbox: one capture, two voids, 19 ledger entries verify.

36
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:06,600
Live voice 24 of 24 synthetic clips. No bid accepted without a confirm.

37
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,900
Webhooks 6 of 6 real sandbox deliveries verified.

38
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:12,000
Latency, honestly. Hammer to captured p95 3.8 s against 2.5 s; to settled 6.9 s against 6 s. Both missed.

39
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:16,000
For judges. One shared judge key, in the Devpost testing instructions. It opens sandbox rooms over plain HTTP. No key is needed for /try.

40
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,800
The key goes into a password field on /try. The docs list every call with a Try-it panel.

41
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,500
gavel.dualmindlab.tech/try. docs.gavel.dualmindlab.tech/docs/judges/call-the-api. api.gavel.dualmindlab.tech

42
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,500
Built with.

43
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,000
PayPal: payments in the PayPal sandbox (Orders v2, Payments v2, webhooks). Built for the PayPal AI Hackathon 2026.

44
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Render: API hosted on Render. Also Cloudflare Workers, AG Grid, Deepgram and Groq. Names only, no endorsement implied.

45
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,100
G3 in progress. The honor-period probe is still timing. The final reading is about 12 Nov.

46
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,600
G5 partial. Speech is measured on synthetic, noise-free audio only.

47
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,000
Sandbox only. No real money moves.

48
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:43,500
Built by Harsh Bhanushali and Dhairya Patel. gavel.dualmindlab.tech. docs.gavel.dualmindlab.tech. github.com/harshbhx/gavel-auction. PayPal sandbox only.
